  "result": "The gate passed node `LVMC_11_38_030` with **OK** (6 witnesses), using 2 of the 6 runs.\n\n**The rule**, in `LVMC_11_38_030.lean`:\n- **Who it covers:** the subject is a motorcycle (`ru_aggregate` with `\"DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle\"`) or a moped (`ru_moped`).\n- **When it applies:** the subject's footprint overlaps some sidewalk region (`rel_occupies`), and `asm.within_city_limits` holds. The sidewalk claim is written as the region kind in that search, because `st_sidewalk` isn't in the list of Boolean atom names.\n- **What it requires:** the subject is at rest (`drv_motion_complete_halt` with `p.halt_speed_tolerance`). Moving while on the sidewalk is a violation.\n\nThe record decided every span, so I declared no narrowings of my own and left the skeleton's declarations unchanged.\n\n**The witnesses** all use the same layout: a roadway beside a sidewalk, and the subject over three instants one second apart.\n\n| Witness | Scene | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | motorcycle at 3 m/s on the sidewalk, inside the city | violated |\n| permit | motorcycle at rest on the sidewalk | compliant |\n| idle | motorcycle at 3 m/s on the roadway | not applicable |\n| blind | motorcycle on the sidewalk, speed not observed | unknown |\n| branch_1 | moped at 2 m/s on the sidewalk | violated |\n| branch_2 | motorcycle at 3 m/s on the sidewalk, outside the city | not applicable |\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. `BUILD_FAIL`: I had given the regions text ids, but region ids are numbers. I changed them to 10 (roadway) and 11 (sidewalk).\n2. `OK`.\n\nThe full report is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
